ncome) rose 10.6% to $141M in 2025. Net interest income rose 9.7% to $106M and noninterest income rose 13.4% to $34.6M; noninterest expense rose 7.0%, and the provision for credit losses was $11.6M, versus $13.2M.","Net income to C&F Financial rose 35.3% to $26.8M, or $8.29 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 68.3% versus 70.6%. C&F Financial returned $6.9M through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 10.6% to $141M.","Net interest income rose 9.7%.","Noninterest income rose 13.4% to $34.6M.","Net income to C&F Financial rose 35.3% to $26.8M."],"watch":["Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was $96.2M, up 7.0%.","Credit-loss provision was $11.6M."],"table":[["Total revenue",0.1408,0.1273,1],["Net interest income",0.1062,0.0968],["Noninterest income",0.0346,0.0305],["Noninterest expense",0.0962,0.0899],["Provision for credit losses",0.0116,0.0132],["Pre-tax income",0.0331,0.0241,1],["Income tax",0.0061,0.0042],["Noncontrolling interests",-0.0002,-0.0001],["Net income to C&F Financial",0.0268,0.0198,1],["Diluted EPS ($)",8.288698,6.011079,0,"eps"],["Book value per share ($)",80.639327,70.000915,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["C&F Financial Corporation Form 10-K filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0000913341&type=10-K"],["C&F Financial financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/cffi/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 75% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 75 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"$141M","sub":"revenue · +10.6%","lines":["Net interest income $106M","Noninterest income $34.6M"],"cap":"Revenue rose 10.6% to $141M.","say":"Revenue rose 10.6% to $141M."},{"kicker":"Per share","big":"$8.29","sub":"diluted EPS · +37.9%","lines":["Net income to C&F Financial $26.8M","Efficiency ratio 68.3%"],"cap":"Diluted EPS rose 37.9% to $8.29.","say":"Diluted earnings per s